module Core

# ============================================================================
# Shared pieces of the correctly rounded B64 sinh and cosh
# ============================================================================
# Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary64/sinh/sinh.c and src/binary64/cosh/cosh.c
# (https://core-math.gitlabpages.inria.fr/), which carry identical copies of these helpers and tables.
# Copyright (c) 2023-2026 Alexei Sibidanov and Paul Zimmermann.
# Copyright (c) 2023-2025 Alexei Sibidanov <sibid@uvic.ca>
# Distributed under the MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH next to this file. RazorForge has no dynamic
# rounding modes, so only the round-to-nearest path of the original is kept. Arithmetic uses the unchecked
# operators `+! -! *! /!`, which are raw IEEE 754 on floats.

# 2^(i/64) for i in 0..63 as a double-double: the high parts, then the low parts (IEEE bit patterns).
# B64_HYP_T1_* holds 2^(i/2^12) for i in 0..63 the same way. tanh uses these tables too.
