### Adds two B64 values exactly when `|x| >= |y|` (or `x == 0`): returns `(s, e)` with `s + e == x + y`.
### :param x: The larger addend.
### :param y: The smaller addend.
### :returns: The rounded sum and its rounding error.
secret routine b64_hyp_fasttwosum(x: B64, y: B64) -> (B64, B64)
  var s = x +! y
  var z = s -! x
  var e = y -! z
  return (s, e)

### Multiplies the double-double `xh + xl` by `ch + cl`, returning the product as a double-double.
### :param xh: The high part of the first factor.
### :param xl: The low part of the first factor.
### :param ch: The high part of the second factor.
### :param cl: The low part of the second factor.
### :returns: The high and low parts of the product.
secret routine b64_hyp_muldd(xh: B64, xl: B64, ch: B64, cl: B64) -> (B64, B64)
  var h = xh *! ch
  var l = (LLVM::fma[B64](a: xh, b: ch, c: -h) +! xh *! cl) +! xl *! ch
  return (h, l)

### Multiplies the double-double `xh + xl` by the double `ch`, returning a double-double.
### :param xh: The high part of the first factor.
### :param xl: The low part of the first factor.
### :param ch: The second factor.
### :returns: The high and low parts of the product.
secret routine b64_hyp_mulddd(xh: B64, xl: B64, ch: B64) -> (B64, B64)
  var h = xh *! ch
  var l = LLVM::fma[B64](a: xh, b: ch, c: -h) +! xl *! ch
  return (h, l)

### The first Horner step of a double-double polynomial: `(c_hi + c_lo) + l`.
### :param l: The value of the higher-degree tail, evaluated in double precision.
### :param c_hi: The high part of the top double-double coefficient.
### :param c_lo: The low part of the top double-double coefficient.
### :returns: The running value as a double-double.
secret routine b64_hyp_polydd_init(l: B64, c_hi: B64, c_lo: B64) -> (B64, B64)
  var s = b64_hyp_fasttwosum(x: c_hi, y: l)
  var cl = s.item1 +! c_lo
  return (s.item0, cl)

### One Horner step of a double-double polynomial: `(ch + cl) * (xh + xl) + (c_hi + c_lo)`.
### :param xh: The high part of the variable.
### :param xl: The low part of the variable.
### :param ch: The high part of the running value.
### :param cl: The low part of the running value.
### :param c_hi: The high part of the next coefficient.
### :param c_lo: The low part of the next coefficient.
### :returns: The new running value as a double-double.
secret routine b64_hyp_polydd_step(xh: B64, xl: B64, ch: B64, cl: B64, c_hi: B64, c_lo: B64) -> (B64, B64)
  var p = b64_hyp_muldd(xh: xh, xl: xl, ch: ch, cl: cl)
  var s = b64_hyp_fasttwosum(x: c_hi, y: p.item0)
  var l = (p.item1 +! c_lo) +! s.item1
  return (s.item0, l)

### Accurate `exp(x)` as a double-double, given the table value `th + tl` of `2^(t/2^12)`.
### :param x: The argument.
### :param t: The integer `round(x * 2^12 / log 2)` as a B64.
### :param th: The high part of `2^(t/2^12)`, already scaled.
### :param tl: The low part of `2^(t/2^12)`, already scaled.
### :returns: The high and low parts of `exp(x)` scaled like `th`.
secret routine b64_hyp_exp_accurate(x: B64, t: B64, th: B64, tl: B64) -> (B64, B64)
  var l2h = 0x1.62e42ffp-13
  var l2l = 0x1.718432a1b0e26p-47
  var l2ll = 0x1.9ff0342542fc3p-102
  var dx = x -! l2h *! t
  var dxl = l2l *! t
  var dxll = l2ll *! t +! LLVM::fma[B64](a: l2l, b: t, c: -dxl)
  var dxh = dx +! dxl
  dxl = ((dx -! dxh) +! dxl) +! dxll
  var fl = dxh *! (0x1.5555555555555p-5 +! dxh *! (0x1.11111113e93e9p-7 +! dxh *! 0x1.6c16c169400a7p-10))
  var p = b64_hyp_polydd_init(l: fl, c_hi: 0x1.5555555555555p-3, c_lo: 0x1.53e93e9f26e62p-57)
  p = b64_hyp_polydd_step(xh: dxh, xl: dxl, ch: p.item0, cl: p.item1, c_hi: 0x1p-1, c_lo: -0x1.8259d904fd34fp-93)
  p = b64_hyp_polydd_step(xh: dxh, xl: dxl, ch: p.item0, cl: p.item1, c_hi: 0x1p+0, c_lo: 0x1.6c16bd194535dp-94)
  p = b64_hyp_muldd(xh: dxh, xl: dxl, ch: p.item0, cl: p.item1)
  p = b64_hyp_muldd(xh: th, xl: tl, ch: p.item0, cl: p.item1)
  var fh = p.item0
  fl = p.item1
  var zh = th +! fh
  var zl = (th -! zh) +! fh
  var uh = zh +! tl
  var ul = ((zh -! uh) +! tl) +! zl
  var vh = uh +! fl
  var vl = ((uh -! vh) +! fl) +! ul
  return (vh, vl)
